  "settingsSelectTodayShiftFromPattern": "Select today's shift from the pattern",
  "settingsScheduleChangeWarning": "Shift alarms for the next 10 days will follow the new schedule. Snoozed alarms and alarm history will be kept.",
  "settingsResetScheduleConfirm": "Reset your shift schedule and all alarms?\n\nAll team schedules, alarm history and alarm creation records will also be deleted.",
  "privacyIntro": "Your shift and alarm data is stored on your device. ShiftBell also uses Google services for usage statistics and advertising. This policy explains those services and local files.",
  "privacyNoCollectionTitle": "Data stored on your device",
  "privacyNoCollectionBody": "Your shifts, alarm settings and history, notes, work hours and overtime are stored in the app’s local database. These contents are not included in analytics events or advertising requests.\n\nOn Android 10 or later, diagnostic files are saved locally in Download/ShiftBell/log. They include device and Android versions, permission and battery settings, and alarm and backup processing records. Note contents and shift names are excluded. The app does not send these files automatically.\n\nSettings → Additional features → Email diagnostic log creates a .txt attachment in the app’s temporary folder. You complete sending in your email app. Sending an email gives the developer the log file, the message you write and your sender email address. ShiftBell does not access your email account information or send logs automatically.\n\nSleep start and end times and confirmation status are also stored on your device. When Sleep & Recovery is enabled, sleep estimation periodically checks screen-off and charging status and processes them on the device. These observations and the contents of sleep records are not sent to a server.",
  "privacyAnalyticsTitle": "Usage statistics (Google Firebase Analytics)",
  "privacyAnalyticsBody": "Google Firebase Analytics collects usage and device information, such as app opens, screen views, app and operating-system versions, device model, approximate region and an installation identifier. ShiftBell also records feature-use events, such as dismissing or snoozing an alarm, saving a note or creating a backup.\n\nThese events do not include shift names, alarm times, note text or other schedule contents. Statistics are processed under Google’s privacy policy.\n\nTo assess app reliability, ShiftBell may send counts of observed alarm scheduling, alarm entry, refresh and device reboot events, categories of permission and battery restrictions, and a device manufacturer category to Google Firebase Analytics. These statistics exclude original diagnostic files, alarm identifiers and times, and the contents of your schedules and notes. Some observations are sent when you next open the app, so reporting dates may differ from occurrence dates.\n\nAnalytics may include events counting use of sleep features, but exclude sleep start and end times and the contents of sleep records.",
  "privacyFirebaseTitle": "App updates",
  "privacyFirebaseBody": "App update availability is checked through Google Play.\n\nEarlier versions may read public update settings from Firebase without including schedule or note contents in the request.",
  "privacyAdsTitle": "Advertising (Google AdMob)",
  "privacyAdsBody": "ShiftBell displays Google AdMob banner ads. The advertising SDK may process device identifiers, IP addresses, app interactions and diagnostics to provide and measure ads. ShiftBell does not include your shift schedule, alarm times or note contents in ad requests.\n\nWhere required by Google’s consent system, the app asks for your advertising choices. When available, use Ad Privacy Settings in Settings to review them. Google’s privacy policy describes how Google handles this information.\n\nThe contents of sleep records are also excluded from ad requests.",
  "privacyPermissionsTitle": "Permissions the app requests",
  "privacyPermissionsBody": "• Notifications: show alarm status and pre-alarm reminders.\n• Display over other apps: show the alarm screen while you use other apps.\n• Exact alarms: schedule alarms for the time you set.\n\nYou can review these permissions in Android Settings. Declining them may limit alarm notifications or prevent alarms from working as expected.\n\n• Lock screen display: allow full-screen notifications to show the alarm screen while the phone is locked.\n\nWhen Sleep & Recovery is enabled, exact alarms are also used to schedule periodic sleep-estimation checks.",
  "privacyDataRetentionTitle": "Data retention and deletion",
  "privacyDataRetentionBody": "Uninstalling removes the app’s local database. Backup and diagnostic files saved in Download/ShiftBell may remain; delete them with your file manager when they are no longer needed.\n\nBackups are not encrypted. They can contain your full local data. Keep them private. The app never uploads these files automatically. If you copy them to a cloud service or send them to someone, that service or recipient controls the copy.\n\nThe app keeps one manual backup and one automatic backup. A new file replaces the previous file of the same kind.\n\nGoogle’s policies apply to retention of analytics and advertising data.\n\nDiagnostic attachments in the app’s temporary folder are removed when the app is uninstalled. Copies you send through email or another app are retained by that service and the recipient.\n\nData created in earlier versions may remain on your device until you delete it or uninstall the app, even if the current interface no longer offers the feature.\n\nThe developer uses emailed support messages, sender email addresses and diagnostic attachments to respond to inquiries and investigate issues, and deletes them within 30 days after the inquiry is resolved. Deletion requests sent to lowvibe07@gmail.com are handled without undue delay. Copies retained separately by the email service are governed by that service’s policy.\n\nBackups also contain sleep records. Turning off Sleep & Recovery or hiding its tab does not delete previously saved sleep records.",
  "privacyChildrenTitle": "Not directed at children",
  "privacyChildrenBody": "This app is not directed at children under 14, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.",
  "privacyContactTitle": "Contact",
  "privacyContactBody": "For app support and privacy questions:\nlowvibe07@gmail.com",
  "privacyEffectiveDate": "Last updated: October 12, 2026.",
  "workHoursNoScheduleYet": "Set up your shift schedule first",
  "workHoursShiftChangeOtTitle": "Extra hours from shift changes",
  "workHoursShiftChangeOtDesc": "When you change a shift in a repeating pattern, count any extra hours as overtime. For example, changing an 8-hour shift to a 12-hour shift adds 4 hours; changing a day off to an 8-hour shift adds 8.\n\nWeekly and monthly work-hour totals always use the updated shift hours. This setting only changes the overtime summary.",
  "workHoursDefaultDurationDesc": "Enter the usual start and end times for each shift. ShiftBell uses them to calculate your scheduled hours and weekly and monthly totals.\n\nIf you enable Sleep & Recovery, these times also help assign sleep records to a shift date and provide guidance for rest between shifts.",
